# Tracked Rust files that no workspace member owns.
#
# Row format: <path> <edition> <reason...>
#
# The edition is stated per row, not inherited from the nearest Cargo.toml,
# because for an out-of-tree file the nearest manifest is not the one it is
# compiled under. Being listed here is not an exemption:
# scripts/lint-rust-fmt-coverage.sh runs `rustfmt --check` on every row, which is
# the coverage `cargo fmt --all` cannot give these files.

npm/lattice-embed-native/build.rs   2024  napi module published to npm from its own manifest, deliberately outside the workspace so the published crate resolves its own dependency tree
npm/lattice-embed-native/src/lib.rs 2024  napi module published to npm from its own manifest, see the row above
scripts/microlora/dsl_validator.rs  2021  links the request-parser crate from a checkout that is not a dependency of this repository; build_dsl_validator.py compiles it in an ephemeral cargo project at edition 2021, so it cannot be a workspace member here and must not be checked at the workspace edition
tests/fixtures/public_api_listing/added/core/src/lib.rs 2024  rustdoc JSON fixture crate for the public API listing tests; each fixture is a standalone workspace so Cargo can generate its own docs
tests/fixtures/public_api_listing/added/facade/src/lib.rs 2024  rustdoc JSON fixture crate for the public API listing tests; each fixture is a standalone workspace so Cargo can generate its own docs
tests/fixtures/public_api_listing/baseline/src/lib.rs 2024  rustdoc JSON fixture crate for the public API listing tests; each fixture is a standalone workspace so Cargo can generate its own docs
